    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "The ぬ series always comes before a noun and does not function as a stand alone like the り series.",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "くま",
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "textStyle",
              "attrs": {
                "color": "var(--secondary-foreground)"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "highlight",
              "attrs": {
                "color": "var(--secondary)"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "んかい　ちゅーん。 To come ",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "(right) here",
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "textStyle",
              "attrs": {
                "color": "var(--secondary-foreground)"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "highlight",
              "attrs": {
                "color": "var(--secondary)"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": ". ((I) come ",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "(right) here",
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "textStyle",
              "attrs": {
                "color": "var(--secondary-foreground)"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "highlight",
              "attrs": {
                "color": "var(--secondary)"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": ").",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "まどぅ　あきーん。",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "うり",
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "textStyle",
              "attrs": {
                "color": "var(--secondary-foreground)"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "highlight",
              "attrs": {
                "color": "var(--secondary)"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "　あきーん。 To open the window. To open ",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "this",
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "textStyle",
              "attrs": {
                "color": "var(--secondary-foreground)"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "highlight",
              "attrs": {
                "color": "var(--secondary)"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": ". ((I) open the window. (I) open ",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "this",
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "textStyle",
              "attrs": {
                "color": "var(--secondary-foreground)"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "highlight",
              "attrs": {
                "color": "var(--secondary)"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "). [The speaker is not touching anything]",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "Note: In this sentence, the this is a standalone instead of an adjective. (Since you are not touching the window, くり is not acceptable in this context. Usually this kind of implies some sort of situation like, I'm closing that window. oh alright, then I'll close this window.)",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "あぬ ",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "くぬ",
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "textStyle",
              "attrs": {
                "color": "var(--secondary-foreground)"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "highlight",
              "attrs": {
                "color": "var(--secondary)"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "　さーたー　かちみーん。To hold ",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "this",
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "textStyle",
              "attrs": {
                "color": "var(--secondary-foreground)"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "highlight",
              "attrs": {
                "color": "var(--secondary)"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " sugar. ((I) hold ",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "this",
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "textStyle",
              "attrs": {
                "color": "var(--secondary-foreground)"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "highlight",
              "attrs": {
                "color": "var(--secondary)"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " sugar) (Since you are holding/touching, くぬ is used for this).",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "Note: あきゆん and かちみゆん are also acceptable alternatives to あきーん and かちみゆん respectively.",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "Also for Japanese speakers, Okinawan くうあ does not perfectly match Japanese こそあ. If you want to read more on this, I'd suggest you'd read 沖縄語初級 book Lesson 2-4.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    }
  ]
}
